What:           /dev/fp_illumination
Date:           October 2026
Contact:        Doctor Logix <doctor.logix@gmail.com>
Description:
                Exclusive root-only (0600) local fingerprint illumination
                control, registered by a panel driver whose panel has an
                optical fingerprint sensor under it. The fd can be passed to
                a trusted compositor; it does not expose arbitrary DSI
                commands or biometric data. Its UAPI is declared in
                linux/fp_illumination.h.

                GET_INFO returns ABI version 1, native panel dimensions, the
                panel's compatible string, panel-on and illumination-active
                state, and the driver's independent maximum activation
                duration. GET_INFO and opening the device do not power the
                panel or change illumination.

                SET accepts a pointer to a u32 (0 disables, 1 enables).
                Enabling requires a prepared, enabled, nonzero-brightness
                panel. Repeated enable cannot extend the activation deadline.
                The caller must wait for presentation scanout before enabling
                and for panel settling before fingerprint acquisition.

                Final close, panel power-down and the independent timeout
                disable local illumination. Failed DSI restoration retains
                active state and schedules a retry; errors must not be treated
                as confirmed restoration. A panel power cycle clears the
                hardware state. The requested normal brightness is restored
                after successful disable, including concurrent brightness
                changes. Unbind invalidates outstanding fds safely.

                Each driver uses its panel's factory local-HBM commands and
                adds no global maximum-brightness fallback:

                oneplus,aston-boe-aa551: factory DBV alpha, OTP-derived gamma
                and local-HBM icon commands, 30000 ms. Normal brightness is
                capped at the factory 900-nit DBV threshold only while the
                region is lit.

                csot,nt37706-v3: the factory local-HBM command set, its
                brightness-band register and DBV alpha table, 30000 ms.
